# Verify before claiming

## The gate

    python3 tools/playtest.py 10

All of these must hold:

- `RESULT: NO ERRORS`
- `sprites resolved: 24/24`
- `main.js: booted=true`, `frames=600`
- `forward-only policy:` **non-zero** — a zero means a lane has become
  unclearable, which is a bug even though nothing threw
- `main.js parse check: PASS`

## The gate does NOT prove appearance

It runs the canvas in JavaScriptCore. It records draw calls and rejects
non-finite coordinates. **It produces no pixels.** A game rendering a black
screen passes it identically to a correct one.

This is not hypothetical. A vignette was verified "structurally valid" and
could not be seen. 734 occlusion inversions were inferred from geometry and
never confirmed. The picker cropped every character top and bottom for an
unknown period while reporting zero errors.

So:

    export PATH="$HOME/.local/node/bin:$PATH"
    python3 -m http.server 8765 --bind 127.0.0.1 &
    node tools/shoot.js http://localhost:8765/select.html /tmp --play

Writes `/tmp/shot_*.png`, prints a canvas pixel histogram and any console
error. **A visual change is verified with a picture, or reported as
unverified.** Do not report a render as working because nothing threw.

## Commit protocol

    git status --porcelain            # clean, or know why not
    python3 tools/playtest.py 10       # before
    # ... work ...
    python3 tools/playtest.py 10       # after
    git commit -m "what changed and why it is observable"

A change that cannot be observed by the gate is not a verified change.
